{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1494802-legacy-requirements-1-or-2-dots","id":1494802,"title":"Legacy Requirements 1 or 2 dots?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-11T12:29:41-07:00","id":1494802,"title":"Legacy Requirements 1 or 2 dots?","content":"Greetings, <br /> <br /> I am confused by the requirements to enter a Legacy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage Awakening Page 197</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Arcane (and Other) Knowledge: </b>Before initiation, your mage must <b>possess at least two dots in the Legacy\u2019s new Ruling Arcanum</b>. She must also possess two dots of Gnosis. If she\u2019s founding her own Legacy, the requirement is increased to three dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the table on Page 199 has the <b>Minimum Legacy Ruling Arcanum</b> at 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So to join or create a legacy, do you need 1 or 2 dots in the Ruling arcanum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-11T15:03:43-07:00","id":1494811,"title":"","content":"Well legally speaking, since the former is for joining/founding Legacied and the latter is for acquiring Attainments, they are different entries\u2026 but setting my inner lawyer aside, I just treat the joining/founding requirement as 2, and this also making all initiates automatically meeting the Arcanum requirements for their First and Second Attainments. (Unless the Legacy has some truly atypical Attainments) Quirky, but not too awkward I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}